    id: 8, module: "Module 1: Android Fundamentals", title: "Resources & Localization",
    type: "theory", duration: "25 min",
    content: `Android's resource system is a powerful mechanism for separating code from configuration, making apps adaptable to different screen sizes, languages, densities, and orientations without changing code logic. All resources are defined in the res/ directory and accessed via the generated R class.\n\nResource Types:\nres/values/strings.xml — Text strings\nres/values/colors.xml — Color definitions\nres/values/dimens.xml — Dimension values\nres/values/themes.xml — App themes and styles\nres/layout/ — UI layout files\nres/drawable/ — Graphics and vector drawables\nres/mipmap/ — App launcher icons\nres/raw/ — Raw files (audio, JSON)\nres/font/ — Custom font files\n\nstrings.xml example:\n<resources>\n  <string name=\"app_name\">EduApp Cameroon</string>\n  <string name=\"welcome_message\">Welcome, %1$s! You have %2$d lessons to complete.</string>\n  <string-array name=\"subjects\">\n    <item>Mathematics</item>\n    <item>Computer Science</item>\n    <item>English</item>\n  </string-array>\n</resources>\n\nUsing resources in Kotlin:\nval appName = getString(R.string.app_name)\nval welcome = getString(R.string.welcome_message, username, lessonCount)\nval subjects = resources.getStringArray(R.array.subjects)\n\nLocalization (Multi-language support):\nCreate alternative resource directories:\nres/values/ — Default (English fallback)\nres/values-fr/ — French resources\nres/values-ar/ — Arabic resources (also use RTL layout)\nres/values-sw/ — Swahili resources\n\nAndroid automatically uses the appropriate resources based on the device's language setting. If no matching resource exists, it falls back to the default.\n\nScreen Density (DPI) qualifiers:\nres/drawable-mdpi/ — Medium density (160dpi) — baseline\nres/drawable-hdpi/ — High density (240dpi) — 1.5x\nres/drawable-xhdpi/ — Extra high (320dpi) — 2x\nres/drawable-xxhdpi/ — 480dpi — 3x\nres/drawable-xxxhdpi/ — 640dpi — 4x\n\nVector drawables (SVG-based) automatically scale to any density — preferred over bitmap images.\n\nScreen Size qualifiers:\nres/layout/ — Default (phones)\nres/layout-sw600dp/ — 600dp smallest width (7\" tablets)\nres/layout-sw720dp/ — 720dp smallest width (10\" tablets)\nres/layout-land/ — Landscape orientation\n\nColor resources (colors.xml):\n<resources>\n  <color name=\"primary\">#4CAF50</color>\n  <color name=\"background\">#FAF7F2</color>\n  <color name=\"text_primary\">#362C28</color>\n</resources>\n\nAccessing in code:\nval primaryColor = ContextCompat.getColor(this, R.color.primary)\n\nNight mode support:\nres/values/themes.xml — Light theme\nres/values-night/themes.xml — Dark theme\nAndroid automatically switches based on system setting.`,
